    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442-a1">

                <pb facs="0567" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg447"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Haitian Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sannon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the American Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note</hi></p>
                <p>In reference to the letter of January 23rd from His Excellency the American
                    Minister and to the plan submitted for the Haitianization of the Garde
                        d’Haiti,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d442-f1"/> the Secretary of State for Foreign
                    Affairs has the honor to submit the enclosed counter-project, prepared by His
                    Excellency the President of the Republic.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-09">February 9, 1931</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="29" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
